Description: Patrone Sans, PatroneOS's interface typeface
 Patrone Sans is a humanist sans of PatroneOS's own, drawn for screens:
 open letters, a large x-height and a little contrast. I, l, 1 and | are
 four different shapes and the zero is plain but narrow, so passwords,
 keys and file names read without mistakes. It has six weights in one
 variable font (light, regular, medium, semibold, bold and black) and
 tabular figures, and covers Latin for Western, Central and Eastern
 European languages; Greek and Cyrillic come from Noto Sans.
 .
 Pick it in Patrone Settings (Theme, Font) or GNOME Settings' Patrone page.
